mainmenu "RTC Alarm Sample"

config RTC_DEMO_SYSTEM_OFF
	bool "Demonstrate wake from system-off via RTC alarm"
	default n
	help
	  When enabled, after the periodic alarm demo completes the system
	  will configure a 10-second RTC alarm and then call sys_poweroff()
	  to enter system-off (deepest sleep, all SRAM lost).
	  The RTC keeps running in system-off and wakes the CPU when the
	  alarm fires, causing the system to cold-boot.

	  The RTC alarm must be set BEFORE sys_poweroff() is called.
	  On wake, the application restarts from main() — there is no
	  resume from sleep; the system performs a full cold boot.

	  Leave disabled (default) to run only the one-shot and periodic
	  alarm demonstrations.

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
